      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So you're saying the concerns about fraud are essentially debunked by these organizations. But if we look at the legal side of it, isn't there a more serious argument to be made about the Tenth Amendment and the constitutional right of states to manage their own elections? It seems like a fundamental principle of federalism. Wouldn't a journalist be remiss if they didn't treat the states' rights argument as a legitimate constitutional debate rather than just a distraction from civil rights issues?",
